Bridge usage analytics to the web client

Settings > Stats & Usage sat on "Not scanned yet" in the tile and the Enable
Claude/Codex/OpenCode buttons did nothing at all - no error, no effect - while
the same build on a Mac shows the full ledger.

`window.api.<provider>Usage.*` is desktop-only IPC that is not in the web
preload, so every call fell through `createFallbackProxy` and resolved to
`undefined`. This adds a `usage.*` RPC family (eight methods, provider as a
parameter) over the stores that already run under `orca serve`, plus three real
preload namespaces. Nothing about scanning changed: the logs, the scanners and
the stores were always on the host, only the pipe was missing. `setEnabled`
mutates the host, so all eight stay off `MOBILE_RPC_METHOD_ALLOWLIST`. Only four
have a symptom in that pane today - the renderer slice batches through
`getSnapshot` - so the rest are specified against the desktop
`<provider>Usage:` IPC handlers they mirror.

The three stores reach the RPC through `src/main/usage/usage-store-registry.ts`,
following the registry upstream introduces at v1.4.190 in `ssh/ssh-target-registry.ts`:
each store is a process singleton owning a cache file and a flush on quit, so a
second instance constructed runtime-side would be a defect, and the registry's
type-only imports keep `electron` out of the runtime graph that
`config/runtime-electron-baseline.txt` requires to stay empty. The runtime itself
therefore never learns that usage exists. An unregistered provider throws
`usage_provider_unavailable:<provider>` rather than answering `undefined` - that
silent `undefined` is the failure this patch removes.

To test, open Settings > Stats & Usage in the tile, enable a provider and scan;
the ledger should match what the same host shows on desktop. Red with this patch
popped: `web-usage-analytics.test.ts` - a case per method - and `usage.test.ts`,
the family's registration. `mobile-rpc-allowlist.test.ts` stays green popped: it
is a patched file, so popping deletes its cases rather than failing them. The
`setUsageProviderStores` call in `main/index.ts` carries no test - nothing here
exercises Electron's entry point.
